Before working on the Egypt / CAI12A project, always read these files in order:

1. `CHATGPT_CURSOR_BASELINE.md`
2. `IMPORTANT_TODO.md`
3. `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md`

Rules:

- Treat GitHub as the shared source of truth.
- Run `git pull` before local work.
- Do not re-implement a fix already committed by ChatGPT; verify it first.
- If Cursor changes CSS, JS, HTML, external resource references, project rules, or the CMS paste version, update `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md` in the same work session.
- If a TODO status changes, update `IMPORTANT_TODO.md`.
- Do not generate the final CMS paste HTML until required tests and status updates are complete, unless the user explicitly asks for a test-only paste version.
- Preserve the approved global exception that hides `#sidebar` and `#sidebar-share-btn`.
- The user should not be asked to manually merge CSS/JS or edit code. Cursor should produce the complete CMS paste HTML.
- When handing work back to ChatGPT, leave exact test results, remaining issues, generated paste filename, and commit SHA in `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md`.
